      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for catching, I\u0027ve amended the dice mode in `fake_dice_artifacts_up_to_pvmfw` as well so that the entire dice chain has a normal mode.\n\nThe mode check was passing anyways because it hit a special case exception: the root certificate was the one with the debug mode, and debug is allowed for root certs if the profile has `allow_root_mode_debug\u003dtrue`.\n\n(Btw, `--allow-any-mode` is the option that allows any mode)\n\nHowever, I decided to run `atest rialto_test` with `allow_root_mode_debug\u003dfalse` to check everything was good, and I saw that the `process_requests_in_protected_vm` test failed (but passed when `allow_root_mode_debug\u003dtrue`). \n\nIs it expected that a protected VM dice chain would have a debug mode root cert (or maybe this is test specific)?",
